## DESCRIPTION
## Given a linear system, write down the augmented coefficient matrix.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('linear system', 'augmented coefficient matrix')

## DBsubject(Linear algebra)
## DBchapter(Systems of linear equations)
## DBsection(Augmented matrices)
## Date(September 5, 2008)
## Institution(Fitchburg State College)
## Author(Peter Staab)


DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',             'PGML.pl',
    'parserImplicitEquation.pl', 'PGmatrixmacros.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("Matrix")->noreduce('(-x)+y', '(-x)-y');

do {
    ($a11, $a12, $a13) = (random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6));
} until $a11 * $a12 != 0 || $a11 * $a13 != 0 || $a12 * $a13 != 0;
do {
    ($a21, $a22, $a23) = (random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6));
} until $a21 * $a22 != 0 || $a21 * $a23 != 0 || $a22 * $a23 != 0;
do {
    ($a31, $a32, $a33) = (random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6), random(-6, 6));
} until $a31 * $a32 != 0 || $a31 * $a33 != 0 || $a32 * $a33 != 0;

$line1 = Formula("$a11 x + $a12 y + $a13 z")->reduce;
$line2 = Formula("$a21 x + $a22 y + $a23 z")->reduce;
$line3 = Formula("$a31 x + $a32 y + $a33 z")->reduce;

$b1 = random(-6, 6);
$b2 = random(-6, 6);
$b3 = random(-6, 6);

$m = Matrix([
    [ $a11, $a12, $a13, $b1 ],
    [ $a21, $a22, $a23, $b2 ],
    [ $a31, $a32, $a33, $b3 ]
]);

BEGIN_PGML
Consider the linear system: 
[```
\begin{aligned}
[$line1] & = [$b1] \\
[$line2] & = [$b2] \\   
[$line3] & = [$b3]
\end{aligned}
```]

Write the linear system as a augmented coefficient matrix. 

[_]*{$m}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
For this, each coefficient is placed in the matrix or:

[``` [$m] ```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();    # This should be the last executable line in the problem.
